# Canon-reviewed: owner approved 2026-10-30 (item 9).
# C25 (#262): ambient talk for Kesselford's 6 posted townsfolk, drafted only from the
# approved proposal (dramgid-vault/proposals/locations/kesselford.md) and the canon documents
# in canon/kesselford/characters/. Titles follow the generated scheme (<town>_<npc_id>);
# TownNpcSpawner routes a roster NPC here when its title exists and otherwise to the generated
# dialogue/kesselford_townsfolk.dialogue, which tools/generate_gloot.gd owns. The band-gated
# greetings are the canon dialogue_hostile / dialogue_warm lines verbatim. No quest content:
# the proposal's side-quest premise is alluded to, never offered, resolved, or flagged.

~ kesselford_kesselford_bell_ringer
if Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "hostile" or Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "cold"
	Hesk Waterward: Bell's not for talk. Move along.
	=> END
elif Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "warm" or Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "allied"
	Hesk Waterward: Water's quiet. Means nothing, but it's quiet.
else
	Hesk Waterward: Mind the bell. If it rings, you stand where you are.
Hesk Waterward: I watch the ford from the bell post and ring when the river rises. Lately it rises on no rain.
Hesk Waterward: Three times this month I have rung it for nothing. I ring it anyway.
- "Why ring on no rain?"
	Hesk Waterward: The river's been moody. That is what we say, and everyone understands.
	Hesk Waterward: A wrong rise is a wrong rise. I ring, and you stand where you are.
	=> END
- "Does anyone answer the bell?"
	Hesk Waterward: The ferries are chained to both banks.
	Hesk Waterward: The Menders sing the ford at dawn, in pairs. After that it is the water's hour.
	=> END
- "I will keep to the bank."
	Hesk Waterward: Cross in the safe hours or sleep on this bank.
	=> END

~ kesselford_kesselford_ferry_keeper
if Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "hostile" or Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "cold"
	Orla Chainwright: You can wait on the bank like everyone else.
	=> END
elif Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "warm" or Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "allied"
	Orla Chainwright: Step aboard; the river's in a listening mood today.
else
	Orla Chainwright: Keep your footing, traveler.
Orla Chainwright: I chain the ferry to both banks before dawn. I read the river's mood before anyone else is awake.
Orla Chainwright: While the water runs the wrong colour, I unchain it for no one.
- "What is the wrong colour?"
	Orla Chainwright: The one you see when you look. I know it, and the chain stays on.
	Orla Chainwright: The river's been moody. Say that and nobody argues.
	=> END
- "Can you not make an exception?"
	Orla Chainwright: Not for coin and not for grain. The chain stays on.
	Orla Chainwright: Cross in the safe hours. There are fewer every year.
	=> END
- "I will wait on the bank."
	Orla Chainwright: Leave me a true count when you return.
	=> END

~ kesselford_kesselford_grain_factor
if Reputation.band("grain-factors-table") == "hostile" or Reputation.band("grain-factors-table") == "cold"
	Factor Wendel Marrow: Unless you can sing a river down, you are no use to me.
	=> END
elif Reputation.band("grain-factors-table") == "warm" or Reputation.band("grain-factors-table") == "allied"
	Factor Wendel Marrow: If you hear the bell go quiet, come find me first.
else
	Factor Wendel Marrow: Mind the bell. If it rings, you stand where you are.
Factor Wendel Marrow: I have waited four days for a safe hour to cross with the Table's grain.
Factor Wendel Marrow: The Table does not pay for waiting. It counts the days all the same.
- "What are you carrying?"
	Factor Wendel Marrow: The Table's grain. It sits on this bank and I sit with it.
	Factor Wendel Marrow: Every hour I wait is an hour the Table writes against me.
	=> END
- "Why not cross anyway?"
	Factor Wendel Marrow: The ferry stays chained while the water runs wrong. I do not argue with a chain.
	Factor Wendel Marrow: The Menders sing the ford at dawn. I stand on the bank and hope the note comes back.
	=> END
- "I will let you wait in peace."
	Factor Wendel Marrow: Cross in the safe hours or sleep on this bank.
	=> END

~ kesselford_kesselford_mender_pair_elder
if Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "hostile" or Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "cold"
	Mender Ivo Threnlow: The charter does not oblige me to speak with you.
	=> END
elif Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "warm" or Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "allied"
	Mender Ivo Threnlow: Walk with us at dawn, if you want to hear what the river says back.
else
	Mender Ivo Threnlow: Mind the bell. If it rings, you stand where you are.
Mender Ivo Threnlow: I sing the ford open every dawn. Lately I sing it only in a pair.
Mender Ivo Threnlow: Someone must be there to catch the note that does not come back.
- "What does the river answer?"
	Mender Ivo Threnlow: Late. A note goes out and the river sends it back after I have stopped listening.
	Mender Ivo Threnlow: I count the ones that come back late. Nessa keeps the count on the map.
	=> END
- "Why sing in pairs?"
	Mender Ivo Threnlow: So one can catch the other when a note does not come back.
	Mender Ivo Threnlow: Phrases hold here, but Songs fray. We sing what holds.
	=> END
- "I will leave you to your counting."
	Mender Ivo Threnlow: Cross in the safe hours or sleep on this bank.
	=> END

~ kesselford_kesselford_mender_pair_junior
if Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "hostile" or Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "cold"
	Mender Nessa Quill: Ivo says I should not talk to you.
	=> END
elif Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "warm" or Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "allied"
	Mender Nessa Quill: The map is honest even when the river is not. Ask me anything.
else
	Mender Nessa Quill: Mind the bell. If it rings, you stand where you are.
Mender Nessa Quill: I keep the Menders' monthly map of where the weather-songs still hold.
Mender Nessa Quill: Ask me how many safe hours the ford lost this year. I will tell you.
- "How many safe hours were lost?"
	Mender Nessa Quill: Fewer than last year, and last year was fewer than the year before. The map shows it month by month.
	Mender Nessa Quill: I do not like writing the new number. I write it anyway.
	=> END
- "Where do the songs still hold?"
	Mender Nessa Quill: Along the ford at dawn, while Ivo and I sing in a pair.
	Mender Nessa Quill: Elsewhere the map shrinks. I redraw it each month.
	=> END
- "I will not keep you from the map."
	Mender Nessa Quill: Cross in the safe hours or sleep on this bank.
	=> END

~ kesselford_kesselford_wayhouse_keeper
if Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "hostile" or Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "cold"
	Dagny Kettlebrook: Beds are full. They are always full for your sort.
	=> END
elif Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "warm" or Reputation.band("wayfare-menders") == "allied"
	Dagny Kettlebrook: A dry bed and a hot kettle. Pay when the river lets you leave.
else
	Dagny Kettlebrook: Mind the bell. If it rings, you stand where you are.
Dagny Kettlebrook: I keep the Ferry Bell Wayhouse, where travellers wait out the ford's moods.
Dagny Kettlebrook: I price a bed by the crossing's mood. I have not had a cheap night since midsummer.
- "Why is it so dear?"
	Dagny Kettlebrook: The crossing is moody, so the bed is dear. The price follows the river.
	Dagny Kettlebrook: When the ferry stays chained, they all stay with me.
	=> END
- "Is there a bed tonight?"
	Dagny Kettlebrook: There is always a bed for someone who can wait.
	Dagny Kettlebrook: Ask how long the ford will keep you, then ask me the price.
	=> END
- "I will see you later."
	Dagny Kettlebrook: Cross in the safe hours or sleep on this bank.
	=> END
